    "final_answer": "I have confirmed all the course details. The page confirms:\n- **Course:** 3D 打印应用 (3D Printing Applications)\n- **University:** University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (renowned US public university)\n- **Instructor:** Vishal Sachdev\n- **Level:** Beginner (初级) - No prior experience needed\n- **Duration:** 1-3 months (confirmed from search results)\n- **Rating:** 4.6 stars (691 reviews)\n- **Enrollment:** 28,771 learners\n- **Modules:** 5 modules\n- **Part of:** \"3D Printing and Additive Manufacturing\" Specialization\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Final Answer\n\nI found a beginner-level online course on **3D printing** that matches all your criteria:\n\n### 🎯 **3D Printing Applications (3D 打印应用)**\n\n| Criterion | Detail |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **Provider** | **University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign** (a renowned US public research university) |\n| **Level** | **Beginner** (初级) — no prior experience required |\n| **Duration** | **1–3 months** (1-3 个月) |\n| **Rating** | 4.6 ★ (691 reviews) |\n| **Enrollment** | 28,771 learners |\n| **Modules** | 5 modules |\n| **Instructor** | Vishal Sachdev |\n| **Link** | https://www.coursera.org/learn/3d-printing-applications |\n\nThis course covers how 3D printing is applied in design, manufacturing, and retail, including special features like customization, self-assembly, and printing complex objects. It is also part of the broader **\"3D Printing and Additive Manufacturing\"** Specialization offered by the same university.\n\n### Other matching alternatives found:\n- **3D Printing Software (三维打印软件)** — University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign · Beginner · 1-3 months · 4.6 ★ (563 reviews)\n- **Rapid Prototyping Using 3D Printing** — Arizona State University · Beginner Specialization · 1-3 months · 4.6 ★ (128 reviews)\n- **Introduction to 3D Printing with Metals** — University of Michigan · Beginner · 1-3 months · 4.8 ★ (21 reviews)",
